    "q-140056": {
      "dom_id": "step-q140056",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Consider the linear transformation $T:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}2x+4y-2z \\\\ -3x-6y+3z \\\\ 4x+8y-4z\\end{aligned}].$ Find $\\,\\text{Ker}(T).$",
      "worked_solution": "Finding the kernel of $T$ is equivalent to finding the null space of the standard matrix of $T.$\n\nFror the given linear transformation, the standard matrix is $T=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ -3 & -6 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 8 & -4\\end{aligned}].$ \n\nSetting $x=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],$ we then need to solve the equation $Tx=0.$ First, we find reduce $T$ to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ -3 & -6 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 8 & -4\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(\\frac{3}{2}){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 8 & -4\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variable is $x$, and we have two free variables, $y,$ and $z.$ That means we need to find $x$ in terms of $y$ and $z.$ \n\nFrom the first equation, we get \n\n$$\nx=-2y+z.\n$$\n\n  \n\nTherefore, the kernel of the linear transformation $\\,T$ is ${[\\begin{aligned}-2y+z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,y,z\\in R}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
